# R1 red proof — 1a/06 denial filter rejects paraphrased denials
# Date: 2026-10-13 (UTC), branch stage-1a-spike, cycle-2 rework follow-up.
# Finding: docs/evidence/1a/qa/cycle2-f3-negative-probe.log probe 4 — the
# denial filter was an allowlist that missed paraphrases ("couldn't be
# reproduced", "unable to reproduce it", "does not reproduce") and let
# them count as observations.
#
# Sabotages: each slipping paraphrase and one newly invented denial as the
# observation in a scratch q03.log (real marker block removed) -> each must
# FAIL with the denial reason. A synthetic genuine phrasing in the same
# scratch shape must pass the marker filter (the check then fails only on
# the standing 4 NOT PERFORMED rows). A curly-apostrophe variant proves the
# normalization. Every scratch state restored with `git checkout --`
# (q03.log is committed) and `git diff --exit-code` clean.

## Standing state (baseline)

$ ACCEPT_STAGE=1a bash scripts/accept/1a/06-spike-answers-complete.sh
CHECK 1a/06-spike-answers-complete: FAIL 4 question(s) NOT PERFORMED (no provider key); stage incomplete
exit=1

